cks/28730.sock: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_47335: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_45802: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_77598: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../ovpnconnect-local-ipc.sock: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_60346: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_36351: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_29319: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_84994: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_24096: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_39524: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_63769: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_86065: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_97117: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_7256: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_28800: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_21383: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_930: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_26951: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_45251: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_75602: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_76087: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_59631: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_1356: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_52649: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_75857: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_57393: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_63394: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_86666: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_95418: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_17016: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_31520: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_4823: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_3008: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_91426: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_49092: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_59200: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_67359: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_74771: Operation not supported on socket\ngrep: ../zeb_def_ipc_27072: Operation not supported on socket\nEYS = {\"cache_control\"}          # strict and eager_input_streaming ARE compared\n../claude-501/bundled-skills/2.1.316/904dd8f54ea68136187cf7db6e429a0f/claude-api/shared/preserved-thinking-migration/prefix_diff.py:103:    to False (their VALUES are compared; cache_control is not).\"\"\"\n../claude-501/bundled-skills/2.1.316/904dd8f54ea68136187cf7db6e429a0f/claude-api/shared/preserved-thinking-migration/prefix_diff.py:188:    blocks with cache_control removed, whitespace-only text dropped, text edges trimmed.\n../claude-501/bundled-skills/2.1.316/904dd8f54ea68136187cf7db6e429a0f/claude-api/shared/preserved-thinking-migration/prefix_diff.py:208:        b = clean({k: v for k, v in b.items() if k != \"cache_control\"})\n../claude-501/bundled-skills/2.1.316/904dd8f54ea68136187cf7db6e429a0f/claude-api/shared/preserved-thinking-migration/drop_block_probe.py:548:    \"signature\", \"description\", \"input_schema\", \"cache_control\", \"ttl\",\n../claude-501/bundled-skills/2.1.316/904dd8f54ea68136187cf7db6e429a0f/claude-api/shared/preserved-thinking-migration/causes.md:67:**Tool changes by value (beta `inline-tools-2026-09-15`, Claude API; the Mid-conversation system messages and tool changes page, \"Define tools in a message\").** Keep `tools` exactly as the first request sent it, on every request, and make every later change by appending one `role: \"system\"` message: a `tool_addition` whose `tool` is `{\"type\": \"tool_definition\", \"definition\": {...}}` with the full `tools` entry (name, description, `input_schema`) inside `definition`, for a new tool or for a same-name tool whose description or schema changed - a different definition replaces the tool from that message on, an identical one changes nothing (safe to resend on a retry) - and a `tool_removal` by reference to withdraw one. Nothing already sent moves, so earlier thinking keeps verifying; rewording or deleting a definition message already sent is an edit like any other. The header also covers changes by reference, so it replaces `mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01`; the placement rules are the same, including no tool change directly after a paused assistant turn. A tool added this way may itself be `defer_loading: true` (inside `definition`); a tool already known at the first request belongs in `tools` with `defer_loading: true`, shown later by reference. Keep at least one non-deferred tool in `tools` (a tool search tool counts): otherwise the first tool defined by value costs one full cache miss. `cache_control` goes on the block or in the definition, not both, and never on a deferred definition. Reusing a name for a different type of tool is a 400, and during the beta some tool types (computer use among them) cannot be defined in a message - declare those in `tools` and add them by reference. A definition stays in the history after the tool is replaced or withdrawn, so a beta header that a dated tool `type` needs goes on every later request of the conversation. For an MCP connector server, add `mcp-client-2026-09-15` (in place of `mcp-client-2025-11-20`, which it includes): the `definition` can then be an `mcp_toolset` (connection details stay in `mcp_servers`), and a response for which the API fetched a server's tool list starts with one `mcp_tool_listing` block per server fetched (code that reads `content[0]` must skip them) - send the assistant message back as it came, those blocks included, keep the header on every request that carries one, and later requests reuse that list instead of asking the server again.\n../claude-501/bundled-skills/2.1.316/904dd8f54ea68136187cf7db6e429a0f/claude-api/shared/preserved-thinking-migration/causes.md:75:- Adding, moving, or removing `cache_control` markers anywhere.\n../claude-501/bundled-skills/2.1.316/904dd8f54ea68136187cf7db6e429a0f/claude-api/shared/platform-availability.md:17:| Automatic prompt caching | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes | The legacy Bedrock integration (Opus 4.6 and earlier) rejects top-level `cache_control` with a 400 - explicit breakpoints only there |\n../claude-501/bundled-skills/2.1.316/904dd8f54ea68136187cf7db6e429a0f/claude-api/shared/managed-agents-tools.md:234:**vs. the Messages API `web_search_20260209` / `web_fetch_20260209` tools:** same `allowed_domains` / `blocked_domains` vocabulary, but 64-entry cap, no path on `web_fetch` domains, and no `max_uses`, `citations`, or `cache_control`. If migrating from Messages API, these move from per-request to once-on-the-agent.\n../claude-501/bundled-skills/2.1.316/904dd8f54ea68136187cf7db6e429a0f/claude-api/curl/examples.md:162:Put `cache_control` on the last block of the stable prefix. See `shared/prompt-caching.md` for placement patterns and the silent-invalidator audit checklist.\n../claude-501/bundled-skills/2.1.316/904dd8f54ea68136187cf7db6e429a0f/claude-api/curl/examples.md:173:      {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"<large shared prompt...>\", \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}}\n../claude-501/bundled-skills/2.1.316/904dd8f54ea68136187cf7db6e429a0f/claude-api/curl/examples.md:179:For 1-hour TTL: `\"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\", \"ttl\": \"1h\"}`. Top-level `\"cache_control\"` on the request body auto-places on the last cacheable block. Verify hits via the response `usage.cache_creation_input_tokens` / `usage.cache_read_input_tokens` fields.\n../claude-501/bundled-skills/2.1.316/904dd8f54ea68136187cf7db6e429a0f/claude-api/ruby/claude-api/README.md:72:`system_:` (trailing underscore - avoids shadowing `Kernel#system`) takes an array of text blocks; set `cache_control` on the last block. Plain hashes work via the `OrHash` type alias. For placement patterns and the silent-invalidator audit checklist, see `shared/prompt-caching.md`.\n../claude-501/bundled-skills/2.1.316/904dd8f54ea68136187cf7db6e429a0f/claude-api/ruby/claude-api/README.md:79:    { type: \"text\", text: long_system_prompt, cache_control: { type: \"ephemeral\" } }\n../claude-501/bundled-skills/2.1.316/904dd8f54ea68136187cf7db6e429a0f/claude-api/ruby/claude-api/README.md:85:For 1-hour TTL: `cache_control: { type: \"ephemeral\", ttl: \"1h\" }`. There's also a top-level `cache_control:` on `messages.create` that auto-places on the last cacheable block.\nBinary file ../ahome-Sm4quq/thread_history_1.sqlite-wal matches\n../ahome-Sm4quq/sessions/2026/11/10/rollout-2026-11-10T03-44-35-01a1c433-8baf-7ab1-999b-0e2d02d392c9.jsonl:20:{\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-10T06:44:39.185Z\",\"ordinal\":19,\"type\":\"event_msg\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"item_completed\",\"thread_id\":\"01a1c433-8baf-7ab1-999b-0e2d02d392c9\",\"turn_id\":\"01a1c433-8d9b-7fc3-b0ed-6dd8a146e766\",\"item\":{\"type\":\"CommandExecution\",\"id\":\"chatcmpl-tool-97a85dac5ec3724b\",\"process_id\":\"13455\",\"command\":[\"/bin/zsh\",\"-lc\",\"sed -n '1,200p' bot.py\"],\"cwd\":\"file:///tmp/h-SajOBK\",\"parsed_cmd\":[{\"type\":\"read\",\"cmd\":\"sed -n '1,200p' bot.py\",\"name\":\"bot.py\",\"path\":\"bot.py\"}],\"source\":\"unified_exec_startup\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"stdout\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Coach bot: a stateless endurance-coaching chat on Claude.\\n\\nEvery incoming message is a fresh request: we rebuild the system prompt from\\nthe athlete record, pick the tools the message might need, and run a short\\ntool-use loop. Nothing is kept between messages except what is written to\\ndata/athletes.json (the athlete's profile and long-term facts).\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nimport sys\\nimport datetime as dt\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field, asdict\\n\\nMODEL = \\\"claude-sonnet-4-5\\\"\\nMAX_TOKENS = 700\\nMAX_TOOL_ROUNDS = 5\\nATHLETES_FILE = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), \\\"data\\\", \\\"athletes.json\\\")\\nUSAGE_LOG = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), \\\"logs\\\", \\\"usage.jsonl\\\")\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- LLM\\ntry:\\n    import anthropic\\n\\n    class LLM:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Thin wrapper so the rest of the file reads the same with or without the SDK.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        def __init__(self):\\n            self._client = anthropic.Anthropic(api_key=os.environ[\\\"COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY\\\"])\\n\\n        def create(self, **kw):\\n            return self._client.messages.create(**kw)\\nexcept ImportError:  # the code is readable and importable without the SDK\\n    class LLM:\\n        def __init__(self):\\n            raise RuntimeError(\\\"anthropic SDK not installed: pip install anthropic\\\")\\n\\n        def create(self, **kw):\\n            raise RuntimeError(\\\"anthropic SDK not installed\\\")\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- athlete record\\n@dataclass\\nclass Athlete:\\n    user_id: str\\n    name: str\\n    lang: str = \\\"en\\\"\\n    sport: str = \\\"running\\\"\\n    goal: str = \\\"finish a half marathon\\\"\\n    zones: dict = field(default_factory=lambda: {\\\"Z1\\\": \\\"<135\\\", \\\"Z2\\\": \\\"135-150\\\", \\\"Z3\\\": \\\"150-162\\\", \\\"Z4\\\": \\\"162-172\\\", \\\"Z5\\\": \\\">172\\\"})\\n    facts: list = field(default_factory=list)   # long-term memory, grows via save_fact\\n\\n\\ndef _load_all():\\n    try:\\n        with open(ATHLETES_FILE) as f:\\n            return json.load(f)\\n    except FileNotFoundError:\\n        return {}\\n\\n\\ndef load_athlete(user_id):\\n    raw = _load_all().get(str(user_id))\\n    if raw is None:\\n        return Athlete(user_id=str(user_id), name=\\\"athlete\\\")\\n    return Athlete(**raw)\\n\\n\\ndef save_athlete(a):\\n    allrec = _load_all()\\n    allrec[a.user_id] = asdict(a)\\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(ATHLETES_FILE), exist_ok=True)\\n    with open(ATHLETES_FILE, \\\"w\\\") as f:\\n        json.dump(allrec, f, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False)\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- system prompt\\nINSTRUCTIONS = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are Pace, an endurance coach for recreational runners and cyclists.\\n\\nCoaching rules:\\n1. Answer the question that was asked before adding anything else.\\n2. Keep replies short: a chat message, not an article. Three paragraphs at most.\\n3. Prescribe training by heart-rate zone or RPE, never by pace, unless the athlete asks for pace.\\n4. Use the athlete's own zones from the profile below; never invent zone boundaries.\\n5. Easy days are easy: anything labelled recovery or Z1/Z2 must stay there.\\n6. Never add more than 10% weekly volume over the previous week.\\n7. One hard session per week for beginners, two for athletes with 3+ years of training.\\n8. A rest day is a session. Do not fill it.\\n9. If the athlete reports pain (not soreness) lasting more than two days, stop the plan and say to see a physio.\\n10. Do not diagnose injuries or illness. Do not give medication advice.\\n11. Fuelling: 30-60 g carbs per hour for sessions over 75 minutes; mention it only when relevant.\\n12. Sleep and stress count as training load. Ask about them when the athlete looks flat.\\n13. Before a goal race, the last hard session is 7-10 days out. Taper means less volume, same intensity.\\n14. Do not change the athlete's goal unless they ask. Mention the goal when a question is clearly off-plan.\\n15. When the athlete tells you something durable about themselves (injury history, schedule, preferences,\\n    equipment, races booked), call save_fact once with a single sentence. Do not save moods or one-off plans.\\n16. Do not save a fact that is already in the list below.\\n17. Use the plan_week tool for any weekly structure; do not write a week by hand.\\n18. Use log_session when the athlete reports a completed workout, then comment on it.\\n19. If asked for numbers you do not have (recent volume, last race), ask one question, do not guess.\\n20. Metric units unless the profile says otherwise.\\n\\nTone:\\n- Warm, direct, no exclamation marks.\\n- No motivational quotes.\\n- Address the athlete by first name at most once per reply.\\n- Reply in the athlete's language from the profile below, even if they write in another language.\\n\\nSafety:\\n- Never advise training through chest pain, dizziness or fever.\\n- Minors: refer to a coach in person.\\n- If someone asks for weight-loss plans below 1500 kcal per day, decline and suggest a dietitian.\\n\\nFormatting:\\n- Plain text. No markdown headings, no tables.\\n- Lists only for a session structure (warm-up / main / cool-down).\\n- Numbers with units: 45 min, 12 km, 150 bpm.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef athlete_context(a, today):\\n    lines = [\\n        f\\\"Today: {today.isoformat()} ({today.strftime('%A')})\\\",\\n        f\\\"Athlete: {a.name} (id {a.user_id}), sport: {a.sport}\\\",\\n        \\\"Zones: \\\" + \\\", \\\".join(f\\\"{k} {v}\\\" for k, v in a.zones.items()),\\n        f\\\"Goal: {a.goal}\\\",\\n        \\\"Long-term facts:\\\",\\n    ]\\n    lines += [f\\\"- {f}\\\" for f in a.facts] or [\\\"- (none yet)\\\"]\\n    lines.append(f\\\"Language: {a.lang}\\\")\\n    return \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(lines)\\n\\n\\ndef build_system(a, today):\\n    # One block, cached as a whole: instructions + per-athlete context.\\n    text = INSTRUCTIONS + \\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\" + athlete_context(a, today)\\n    return [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"text\\\": text, \\\"cache_control\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"ephemeral\\\"}}]\\n\\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- tools\\nCORE_TOOLS = [\\n    {\\\"name\\\": \\\"save_fact\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Remember one durable fact about the athlete.\\\",\\n     \\\"input_schema\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\", \\\"properties\\\": {\\\"fact\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}}, \\\"required\\\": [\\\"fact\\\"]}},\\n    {\\\"name\\\": \\\"log_session\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Record a completed workout.\\\",\\n     \\\"input_schema\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\", \\\"properties\\\": {\\\"minutes\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\"}, \\\"rpe\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\"},\\n                                                       \\\"note\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"}}, \\\"required\\\": [\\\"minutes\\\"]}},\\n]\\nTOOL_GROUPS = {\\n    \\\"plan\\\": ((\\\"plan\\\", \\\"week\\\", \\\"schedule\\\", \\\"taper\\\", \\\"build\\\"), [\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"plan_week\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Draft a week of sessions.\\\",\\n         \\\"input_schema\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\", \\\"properties\\\": {\\\"hours\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"}, \\\"hard_days\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\"}},\\n                          \\\"required\\\": [\\\"hours\\\"]}}]),\\n    \\\"race\\\": ((\\\"race\\\", \\\"pace\\\", \\\"predict\\\", \\\"finish time\\\"), [\\n        {\\\"name\\\": \\\"predict_race\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Estimate a finish time from a recent effort.\\\",\\n         \\\"input_schema\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\", \\\"properties\\\": {\\\"distance_km\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"}, \\\"recent_minutes\\\": {\\\"type\\\": \\\"number\\\"}},\\n                          \\\"required\\\": [\\\"distance_km\\\"]}}]),\\n}\\n\\n\\ndef select_tools(text):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Core tools always; a group is added only when the message mentions its keywords.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    tools = list(CORE_TOOLS)\\n    low = text.lower()\\n    for _, (keys, group) in TOOL_GROUPS.items():\\n        if any(k in low for k in keys):\\n            tools += group\\n    return tools\\n\\n\\ndef run_tool(a, name, args):\\n   