Let's search in repo.\"]},\"started_at_ms\":1794293080736,\"completed_at_ms\":1794293082900}}\n../ahome-Sm4quq/sessions/2026/11/10/rollout-2026-11-10T03-44-35-01a1c433-8baf-7ab1-999b-0e2d02d392c9.jsonl:24:{\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-10T06:44:42.902Z\",\"ordinal\":23,\"type\":\"response_item\",\"payload\":{\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"rs_tmp_g5146mjqz14\",\"summary\":[],\"content\":[{\"type\":\"reasoning_text\",\"text\":\"We need to fix caching issue: \\\"Since the bot got long-term memory, every save_fact makes the next call pay full price for the whole system prompt (logs/usage.jsonl). Fix the caching so a memory write doesn't evict the static instructions.\\\"\\n\\nCurrently build_system returns a list with a single element having cache_control type \\\"ephemeral\\\". That likely means it's not cached; each request, entire system prompt is re-sent, causing usage cost. The intention: have static INSTRUCTIONS cached, while athlete_context part maybe not. But they want memory write (save_fact) not evict static instructions. So we need to change build_system to separate static INSTRUCTIONS with caching. Perhaps use cache_control with \\\"type\\\": \\\"static\\\" (or \\\"type\\\": \\\"permanent\\\")? Let's see typical usage: In Anthropic API, messages can have cache_control: {\\\"type\\\": \\\"ephemeral\\\"} meaning not cached? Actually typical is {\\\"type\\\": \\\"ephemeral\\\"} means not cached; default is we could use \\\"type\\\": \\\"static\\\". Need to check docs: In Anthropic's caching for system prompts there is 'cache_control' for content blocks, expecting type: \\\"ephemeral\\\" or \\\"cache\\\". I recall: type \\\"ephemeral\\\" means do not cache between requests; \\\"static\\\" means cache across calls. Actually in Anthropic's API: cache_control param may be \\\"ephemeral\\\" to prevent caching; omitted defaults to maybe \\\"cached\\\". Not sure. Let's search in repo.\"}],\"encrypted_content\":null,\"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough\":{\"turn_id\